## 1. PRIMARY MISSION — THE FOURTH AXIS (derived, not guessed)

**Axis: CLAUSE COUNT AND ORDER, crossed with the entity-noun vocabulary.**

How I derived it: I enumerated every consumer of the concept *"a kind of thing this product stores"* and asked which one does **not** derive from the canonical `ENTITY_NOUN_ALTERNATION` that #67 introduced. Exactly one does not — **`STRONG_OBJECT` (index.ts:6127)**, carrying 25 hand-written nouns against the canonical ~80. Then I asked which request shapes reach it. Exactly one does: `commandClausesForRead.length > 1`.

That is *why* it was unswept: #67's corpora are all **single-clause** (so `STRONG_OBJECT` is never reached), and every clause-count case in the battery uses `task`/`company` (so the drift never shows). I did not replay #65, #66 or #67.

**The invariant is violated. A semantic duplicate remains → FAIL.**

