## 2. REQUEST CONSISTENCY, BOTH DIRECTIONS — the false-positive half is also broken

### V65-D2 (P1) — **introduced by this candidate**

#148's repair "a referring token counts wherever it sits" was implemented **position-free**. An English noun-phrase headline whose head word is one of the ~120 lexicon verbs almost always contains an entity noun, so it becomes "an imperative with a referring object" — and the receipt then **deletes the truthful answer**:

> `"Transfer pricing for the business unit"` → *"No change was made — that request did not resolve to an operation I can execute from chat."*

| vs the #67 parent `916da4e2` | parent | candidate |
|---|---|---|
| Truthful reads acquiring mutation intent | 2/40 | **31/40** |
| Truthful answers destroyed | 1/8 | **8/8** |

The implementing session found and reverted *one* member of this class (capitalised-word-anywhere) and kept the other, which has the same disease. **This is a truth regression vs v92, and it is not an intended departure** — §3 rule 2 forbids text shape being the sole reason a response is rewritten.

The two P1s are one defect wearing two faces: the vocabulary was shared in the tier that needed a position rule, and the position rule was dropped in the tier that needed the vocabulary.

